hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27897","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym, narrated to us, he said: Tawus narrated to me, from Umm Malik al-Bahziyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of people in tribulation is a man secluded with his wealth, worshipping his Lord and rendering its due, and a man holding the head of his horse in the path of Allah, frightening them and they frightening him."
